A worker finishes its running job on SIGTERM

Why: StartWorkerShell installs no signal handler, so SIGTERM ends the worker at once and its running job stays at status 0. With the handler the worker takes no new job and exits once the running one ends; the supervisor (files/misp_container/worker.py) waits WORKER_STOP_GRACE for it. The signal also interrupts the stream_select() in BackgroundJob::pool(), which then threw "Could not select stream" and failed the job; the pool selects again. An idle worker waits in BLPOP, which phpredis resumes after a signal, so its timeout drops from 30 s to 5 s.
Upstream: not filed yet

